      "crowdsourced_ai_results": [
        {
          "analysis": "The sample exhibits behaviors typical of an obfuscated malware loader or crypter. It employs control flow obfuscation by routing its execution stages through a GUI window procedure using SendMessageA with custom command IDs (e.g., 0x36, 0x3a, 0x3b). It dynamically resolves Windows APIs by manually traversing the export directories of loaded modules in memory, searching for the 'MZ' header (0x5a4d) to bypass Import Address Table (IAT) monitoring. Furthermore, the binary contains custom decryption/decompression routines and heavily obfuscated functions containing junk instructions (e.g., __das, __daa) designed to hinder static analysis. It also interacts with a file named 'last.inf', which likely acts as an external payload or configuration file.",
          "verdict": "malicious",
